So since valkyries are apparently the only role I'm capable
of ascending (I've been playing barbarians this whole month,
but they all seem to get killed by eels or choking), I decided
to use them for my first "real" conduct game.

Random musings:
1) Apparently AC -18 is enough for any valkyrie with Orb of
Fate and a ring of conflict to survive the Sanctum and Planes,
barring any super-bad luck.  I only got engulfed twice on the
Plane of Air, and my HP never dropped below 200.  I also
discovered wands of slow monster help a lot with evading the
air elementals, especially if you're very fast and only a few of
them are chasing you.

2) After I cleared out Mines' End, a soldier dropped a wand
of wishing on dlvl6.  (Hint: screaming for joy will make
roommates think you are weird.)  I used the engrave-wish
for silver dragon scale mail (already had CoMR from early
bones file) and saved the other wishes for CoMR, =oLev
and speed boots later in the game.  (Damn you, potions
of polymorph!)  I also found two magic lamps in Hell, but
none of them gave me a wish...

3) Playing Elberethless makes mind flayers a huge pain in
the ass.  But then again, none of my inventory was really
identified anyway, and I'd dug out paths between the stairs
in Gehennom, so it wasn't as bad as it could have been.
Liches were fun though since I could use them to find the
upstairs..and whenever they summoned things, a cockatrice
seemed to be nearby.

4) Oh, and whenever I named things instead of calling them, I
never seemed to forget what I named them...is that normal?
It certainly helped when I was trying to reidentify stuff and I
had this amulet named "Vlad..."

5) I kept my original pet until the Castle (occasionally losing
him) to test for good armor.  This was probably why it took me
44760 turns to *get* past the Castle.  I hope atheist doesn't
take as long as illiterate did..

6) I prayed for unholy water in the Valley of the Dead and lost
protection...does this happen on any crossaligned altar or is it
just because I prayed in Gehennom?

